<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch BNG says H1 profit rose four pct.</title>
<headline>Dutch BNG says H1 profit rose four pct.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch local authorities bank Bank Nederlandse Gemeenten (BNG) said on Tuesday profits rose to 168 million guilders in the first half of 1997, up four percent from 162 million in the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>The bank, which is a major borrower on international capital markets, said the full year profit would be higher than the previous year.</p>
<p>BNG is owned by the Dutch state, provinces and towns.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
